  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2017-09-27T23:39:10.849Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "We've been using the Moderation Channel on Discord for logging bad players and for emergencies, but I think we should have a more solid way of reporting players.\n\nMy idea is that we would still keep the Discord Channel for emergencies and logging stuff, but have some sort of website or even on the VRChat website itself a way of filling down a Template/Form for reporting players, it would REQUIRE us to be logged in to our VRChat account so it says who's reporting it and all that and we could have a simple form like:\n- Reported User(s)/Player(s) Usernames(s)\n- Time(s) & Date(s) (optional)\n- Details/Info\n- Proof (Media)\n\n---------\n\nThese reports would be into a Ticket kind of System so Moderators can handle them well and 'claim' them so they deal with it and go from there, they can archive the reports and have them ready for future references if needed, also possibility to filter reported names to see how many time someone got reported etc...",
